# What the model is told after a command the user stopped: Ctrl-C while a
# six-second command runs (as in interrupt-cmd), then, once the command would
# have ended, a new prompt -- the request it sends is the receipt (gwlog).
fx: gateway interrupt-cmd-fx.json
xfx: gateway interrupt-cmd-xfx.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
# The full-access warning is up from the first frame (capfile.py TIMERS):
# seen here, so the `until gone` before the Ctrl-C below is its going and
# not a look taken before it came.
until shown Full access
wait 2
type run cmd
key Enter
wait 2.5
# A Ctrl-C while the full-access warning is up takes its row and stops its
# 4 s clock (capfile.py TIMERS), so the warning would come back once the
# exit hint goes: Ctrl-C is sent once the warning has gone.
until gone Full access
key C-c
wait 7
type next
key Enter
wait 2.5
snap next
gwlog
